1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:07,375
MARCUS: No, tell them nine sharp. I've got the deck, I've got the clicker. Brenda... today is MY day.

2
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:10,225
LEONARD: Bless you.

3
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:12,948
MARCUS: Sorry. No, the BLUE slides.

4
00:00:13,548 --> 00:00:14,599
LEONARD: ...Bless you.

5
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:18,705
LEONARD: Bless. You.

6
00:00:19,055 --> 00:00:20,829
MARCUS: I HEARD you, man!

7
00:00:21,279 --> 00:00:23,127
LEONARD: Then where's my thank-you?

8
00:00:23,477 --> 00:00:26,550
MARCUS: It's a reflex! It's just a thing people say.

9
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:33,059
LEONARD: I don't say things. I blessed you. I reached in, and I gave you some of mine.

10
00:00:33,559 --> 00:00:38,009
LEONARD: Everybody says thank you. I blessed a horse once. He nodded.

11
00:00:38,509 --> 00:00:40,136
MARCUS: Well, I'm not a horse.

12
00:00:40,486 --> 00:00:42,645
LEONARD: No. The horse had manners.

13
00:00:43,445 --> 00:00:47,312
MARCUS: Okay. Well. I'm good. I'm all set on blessings.

14
00:00:47,662 --> 00:00:49,291
LEONARD: So you don't want it.

15
00:00:49,641 --> 00:00:51,495
MARCUS: I don't NEED it.

16
00:00:54,195 --> 00:00:55,999
LEONARD: Then I'll be taking it back.

17
00:00:56,249 --> 00:00:58,919
MARCUS: You'll be... how do you take back a...

18
00:01:00,869 --> 00:01:02,368
MARCUS: Is that coming out of ME?

19
00:01:02,618 --> 00:01:04,797
LEONARD: Don't pull. You'll stretch it.

20
00:01:06,897 --> 00:01:07,966
LEONARD: Un-bless you.

21
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:13,293
MARCUS: Wow. Okay. Devastating.

22
00:01:13,593 --> 00:01:16,296
MARCUS: What's next, you gonna un-hold a door?

23
00:01:16,696 --> 00:01:18,056
LEONARD: Don't tempt me.

24
00:01:21,656 --> 00:01:22,356
MARCUS: Really?

25
00:01:27,079 --> 00:01:28,904
MARCUS: ...That's a coincidence.

26
00:01:29,404 --> 00:01:32,405
LEONARD: Six letters. Hubris.

27
00:01:33,905 --> 00:01:39,992
MARCUS: Hey bud. Going with Greg for the presentation. Also, Greg's taking your office. Also, your chair.

28
00:01:40,292 --> 00:01:41,549
MARCUS: My CHAIR?

29
00:01:44,499 --> 00:01:47,420
MUM: Don't stare, darling. He's got no blessing.

30
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:48,864
MARCUS: I'm FINE!

31
00:01:50,764 --> 00:01:52,339
MARCUS: Mom. Hey.

32
00:01:52,739 --> 00:02:01,788
MOM: Marcus, sweetheart. I don't know why, but I just had the strongest urge to call and tell you... I've always preferred your brother.

33
00:02:04,288 --> 00:02:07,578
MOM: Okay! Love you. Well... you know.

34
00:02:09,278 --> 00:02:12,697
MARCUS: Okay. Okay! Thank you. THANK you. There.

35
00:02:13,197 --> 00:02:13,897
LEONARD: For what?

36
00:02:14,391 --> 00:02:18,426
MARCUS: Thank you for blessing me, sir, when I sneezed. Can I have it back?

37
00:02:18,926 --> 00:02:24,966
LEONARD: It's not that simple. The original was complimentary. This would be a re-blessing.

38
00:02:25,266 --> 00:02:26,296
MARCUS: What's the difference?

39
00:02:26,696 --> 00:02:27,485
LEONARD: Paperwork.

40
00:02:28,085 --> 00:02:32,269
LEONARD: In the past twelve months, have you declined any other courtesies?

41
00:02:32,769 --> 00:02:35,870
MARCUS: ...A guy held a door. I was on my phone.

42
00:02:36,270 --> 00:02:38,043
LEONARD: Mmm.

43
00:02:38,443 --> 00:02:39,753
MARCUS: What's 'mmm'?

44
00:02:40,103 --> 00:02:41,827
LEONARD: It's a pattern, Marcus.

45
00:02:42,427 --> 00:02:44,076
MARCUS: How do you know my name?

46
00:02:44,576 --> 00:02:45,787
LEONARD: It's on your lanyard.

47
00:02:47,287 --> 00:02:48,990
LEONARD: Now. Which package?

48
00:02:49,290 --> 00:02:50,048
MARCUS: ...Package?

49
00:02:50,348 --> 00:02:53,615
LEONARD: Standard. 'Bless you.' Gets the job done.

50
00:02:53,915 --> 00:02:57,606
LEONARD: Premium. 'God bless you.' Comes with God.

51
00:02:58,006 --> 00:03:04,254
LEONARD: Imported. 'Gesundheit.' German. Very efficient. Works before you've finished sneezing.

52
00:03:04,654 --> 00:03:06,114
MARCUS: That's not possible.

53
00:03:06,414 --> 00:03:07,339
LEONARD: Germans.

54
00:03:07,939 --> 00:03:11,104
LEONARD: And our regional option... 'Bless your heart.'

55
00:03:11,454 --> 00:03:13,938
MARCUS: Ooh. That one sounds nice.

56
00:03:14,388 --> 00:03:15,408
LEONARD: It's an insult.

57
00:03:16,308 --> 00:03:18,161
MARCUS: Just the standard!

58
00:03:18,511 --> 00:03:24,853
LEONARD: I'll need three thank-yous. One for the original. One for my time. And one in advance.

59
00:03:25,203 --> 00:03:26,878
MARCUS: Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

60
00:03:27,228 --> 00:03:30,086
LEONARD: Those were to the pavement. In my eyes.

61
00:03:31,886 --> 00:03:32,586
MARCUS: Thank you.

62
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:35,756
LEONARD: Was that so hard?

63
00:03:36,156 --> 00:03:38,224
MARCUS: So we're good. I'm re-blessed.

64
00:03:38,624 --> 00:03:41,372
LEONARD: Now I just need my supervisor to sign off.

65
00:03:41,672 --> 00:03:43,017
MARCUS: Your SUPERVISOR?

66
00:03:44,617 --> 00:03:45,977
DENISE: Mm-hm.

67
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:48,967
DENISE: Approved. Pending a sneeze.

68
00:03:49,267 --> 00:03:51,512
MARCUS: How long have you been his supervisor?

69
00:03:51,812 --> 00:03:55,198
DENISE: Forty years. He's on a performance plan.

70
00:03:55,698 --> 00:03:56,969
MARCUS: Pending a WHAT?

71
00:03:57,269 --> 00:04:00,594
LEONARD: Oh, I can't bless you. You'd have to sneeze.

72
00:04:00,894 --> 00:04:02,904
LEONARD: And my bus is in one minute.

73
00:04:05,054 --> 00:04:06,933
MARCUS: Ah... choo.

74
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:11,068
LEONARD: I'm not blessing that. That was a man saying achoo.

75
00:04:11,368 --> 00:04:13,212
LEONARD: Thirty seconds.

76
00:04:16,412 --> 00:04:20,853
MARCUS: Wait, wait, wait! It's coming! Ah... AH... AAAH...

77
00:04:22,753 --> 00:04:23,697
MARCUS: ...I lost it.

78
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:24,997
LEONARD: Mmm.

79
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:34,278
LEONARD: ...Marcus.

80
00:04:37,578 --> 00:04:40,633
MARCUS: Brenda! Hey. No, no. Now's perfect.

81
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:51,731
DENISE: Bless his heart.
